/a> · <a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" data-wpel-link="internal" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Revelation/19/7-8" title="Open Revelation 19:7-8 in Bible Search">Revelation 19:7-8</a></p></div></div></details><details class="group border-line overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border bg-white shadow-[0_8px_24px_rgba(62,9,63,0.05)]"><summary class="hover:bg-purple-soft flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 px-5 py-4 transition sm:px-6 [&amp;::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden"><span class="font-display text-purple-deep text-lg leading-snug sm:text-xl">74 - The Word of the Lord in Jerusalem (Isaiah 2)</span><span class="bg-purple-soft text-purple-deep flex size-8 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full"><svg aria-hidden="true" class="lucide lucide-chevron-down size-4 transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-180" fill="none" height="24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" viewbox="0 0 24 24" width="24" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"></path></svg><span class="sr-only">Toggle passage</span></span></summary><div class="border-line video-rail max-h-[22rem] overflow-y-auto overscroll-contain border-t px-5 py-5 sm:px-6"><div class="space-y-4"><p class="text-ink text-base leading-8 whitespace-pre-line"><a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" data-wpel-link="internal" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Isaiah/2/1-5" title="Open Isaiah 2:1-5 in Bible Search">Isaiah 2:1-5</a>
1: The word which Isaiah the son of Amoz saw concerning Judah and Jerusalem. 2: It shall come to pass in the latter days that the mountain of the house of the LORD shall be established as the highest of the mountains, and shall be raised above the hills; and all the nations shall flow to it, 3: and many peoples shall come, and say: “Come, let us go up to the mountain of the LORD, to the house of the God of Jacob; that he may teach us his ways and that we may walk in his paths.” For out of Zion shall go forth the law, and the word of the LORD from Jerusalem. 4: He shall judge between the nations, and shall decide for many peoples; and they shall beat their swords into plowshares, and their spears into pruning hooks; nation shall not lift up sword against nation, neither shall they learn war any more. 5: O house of Jacob, come, let us walk in the light of the LORD.</p><p class="text-ink text-base leading-8 kjt-pm__ful kjt-pf"><strong>Fulfilled in Christ:</strong> <a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" data-wpel-link="internal" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Luke/24/47" title="Open Luke 24:47 in Bible Search">Luke 24:47</a> · <a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" data-wpel-link="internal" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Acts/1/8" title="Open Acts 1:8 in Bible Search">Acts 1:8</a></p></div></div></details><details class="group border-line overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border bg-white shadow-[0_8px_24px_rgba(62,9,63,0.05)]"><summary class="hover:bg-purple-soft flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 px-5 py-4 transition sm:px-6 [&amp;::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden"><span class="font-display text-purple-deep text-lg leading-snug sm:text-xl">ETYMOLOGY</span><span class="bg-purple-soft text-purple-deep flex size-8 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full"><svg aria-hidden="true" class="lucide lucide-chevron-down size-4 transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-180" fill="none" height="24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" viewbox="0 0 24 24" width="24" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"></path></svg><span class="sr-only">Toggle passage</span></span></summary><div class="border-line video-rail max-h-[22rem] overflow-y-auto overscroll-contain border-t px-5 py-5 sm:px-6"><div class="space-y-4"><p class="text-ink text-base leading-8 whitespace-pre-line">Jesus (God Saves)
Yah (God) Suu (Saves)</p><p class="text-ink text-base leading-8 whitespace-pre-line">Emanuel (God with us):
Emanu (With us) El (God)</p><p class="text-ink text-base leading-8 whitespace-pre-line">Messiah / Christ:
The Anointed One</p><p class="text-ink text-base leading-8 whitespace-pre-line">For in Him dwells all the fullness of the Godhead bodily
<a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" data-wpel-link="internal" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Colossians/2/9" title="Open Colossians 2:9 in Bible Search">Colossians 2:9</a></p></div></div></details></div></div></div></div></section><section class="bg-paper border-line border-t scroll-mt-20 kjt-x-sec" id="christ-in-the-old-testament"><div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-5 py-14 sm:px-8 sm:py-20"><div class="mb-10 max-w-3xl"><p class="text-purple text-xs font-bold tracking-[0.22em] uppercase">Before Bethlehem</p><h2 class="font-display text-purple-deep mt-3 text-4xl leading-tight sm:text-5xl">Christ in the Old Testament</h2><p class="text-ink mt-5 text-lg leading-8">The Son of God was at work long before He was born of the Virgin. Again and again “the Angel of the Lord” speaks as God, swears by Himself, receives worship and is called God. With the holy Fathers, the Church sees in Him the Son, the Word of God: “angel” means messenger, and the Son is the One sent by the Father. In the Greek Old Testament Isaiah calls Him “the Angel of great counsel” (Isaiah 9:6).</p></div><div class="kjt-x-grid grid gap-5"><article class="border-line rounded-3xl border bg-white p-6 sm:p-7"><h3 class="font-display text-purple-deep text-2xl leading-tight">Hagar: “Thou God seest me”</h3><div class="kjt-x mt-3"><blockquote class="kjt-x-v"><p>And the angel of the LORD said unto her, I will multiply thy seed exceedingly, that it shall not be numbered for multitude. And the angel of the LORD said unto her, Behold, thou art with child, and shalt bear a son, and shalt call his name Ishmael; because the LORD hath heard thy affliction. And he will be a wild man; his hand will be against every man, and every man’s hand against him; and he shall dwell in the presence of all his brethren. And she called the name of the LORD that spake unto her, Thou God seest me: for she said, Have I also here looked after him that seeth me?</p><cite><a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Genesis/16/10-13">Genesis 16:10-13</a></cite></blockquote><p class="text-ink text-base leading-8">The Angel promises what only God can promise, and Hagar names Him God.</p></div></article><article class="border-line rounded-3xl border bg-white p-6 sm:p-7"><h3 class="font-display text-purple-deep text-2xl leading-tight">Abraham on Mount Moriah</h3><div class="kjt-x mt-3"><blockquote class="kjt-x-v"><p>And the angel of the LORD called unto him out of heaven, and said, Abraham, Abraham: and he said, Here am I. And he said, Lay not thine hand upon the lad, neither do thou any thing unto him: for now I know that thou fearest God, seeing thou hast not withheld thy son, thine only son from me.</p><cite><a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Genesis/22/11-12">Genesis 22:11-12</a></cite></blockquote><blockquote class="kjt-x-v"><p>And the angel of the LORD called unto Abraham out of heaven the second time, And said, By myself have I sworn, saith the LORD, for because thou hast done this thing, and hast not withheld thy son, thine only son:</p><cite><a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Genesis/22/15-16">Genesis 22:15-16</a></cite></blockquote><p class="text-ink text-base leading-8">The Angel speaks of Isaac as offered to Himself, and swears by Himself as the Lord.</p></div></article><article class="border-line rounded-3xl border bg-white p-6 sm:p-7"><h3 class="font-display text-purple-deep text-2xl leading-tight">Jacob: “I am the God of Bethel”</h3><div class="kjt-x mt-3"><blockquote class="kjt-x-v"><p>And the angel of God spake unto me in a dream, saying, Jacob: And I said, Here am I. And he said, Lift up now thine eyes, and see, all the rams which leap upon the cattle are ringstraked, speckled, and grisled: for I have seen all that Laban doeth unto thee. I am the God of Beth-el, where thou anointedst the pillar, and where thou vowedst a vow unto me: now arise, get thee out from this land, and return unto the land of thy kindred.</p><cite><a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Genesis/31/11-13">Genesis 31:11-13</a></cite></blockquote></div></article><article class="border-line rounded-3xl border bg-white p-6 sm:p-7"><h3 class="font-display text-purple-deep text-2xl leading-tight">Jacob wrestles: “I have seen God face to face”</h3><div class="kjt-x mt-3"><blockquote class="kjt-x-v"><p>And Jacob asked him, and said, Tell me, I pray thee, thy name. And he said, Wherefore is it that thou dost ask after my name? And he blessed him there. And Jacob called the name of the place Peniel: for I have seen God face to face, and my life is preserved.</p><cite><a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Genesis/32/29-30">Genesis 32:29-30</a></cite></blockquote><p class="text-ink text-base leading-8">Peniel means “the face of God”. Jacob later blesses his grandsons in the name of “the Angel which redeemed me from all evil”.</p><blockquote class="kjt-x-v"><p>And he blessed Joseph, and said, God, before whom my fathers Abraham and Isaac did walk, the God which fed me all my life long unto this day, The Angel which redeemed me from all evil, bless the lads; and let my name be named on them, and the name of my fathers Abraham and Isaac; and let them grow into a multitude in the midst of the earth.</p><cite><a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Genesis/48/15-16">Genesis 48:15-16</a></cite></blockquote></div></article><article class="border-line rounded-3xl border bg-white p-6 sm:p-7"><h3 class="font-display text-purple-deep text-2xl leading-tight">Moses at the burning bush</h3><div class="kjt-x mt-3"><blockquote class="kjt-x-v"><p>And the angel of the LORD appeared unto him in a flame of fire out of the midst of a bush: and he looked, and, behold, the bush burned with fire, and the bush was not consumed. And Moses said, I will now turn aside, and see this great sight, why the bush is not burnt. And when the LORD saw that he turned aside to see, God called unto him out of the midst of the bush, and said, Moses, Moses. And he said, Here am I. And he said, Draw not nigh hither: put off thy shoes from off thy feet, for the place whereon thou standest is holy ground. Moreover he said, I am the God of thy father, the God of Abraham, the God of Isaac, and the God of Jacob. And Moses hid his face; for he was afraid to look upon God.</p><cite><a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Exodus/3/2-6">Exodus 3:2-6</a></cite></blockquote><p class="text-ink text-base leading-8">The Angel of the Lord in the flame is the One who says “I am the God of Abraham”, and a few verses later “I AM THAT I AM”. Christ said: “Before Abraham was, I am” (John 8:58).</p></div></article><article class="border-line rounded-3xl border bg-white p-6 sm:p-7"><h3 class="font-display text-purple-deep text-2xl leading-tight">“My name is in Him”</h3><div class="kjt-x mt-3"><blockquote class="kjt-x-v"><p>Behold, I send an Angel before thee, to keep thee in the way, and to bring thee into the place which I have prepared. Beware of him, and obey his voice, provoke him not; for he will not pardon your transgressions: for my name is in him.</p><cite><a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Exodus/23/20-21">Exodus 23:20-21</a></cite></blockquote><p class="text-ink text-base leading-8">This Angel can forgive or not forgive sins, and the very name of God is in Him.</p></div></article><article class="border-line rounded-3xl border bg-white p-6 sm:p-7"><h3 class="font-display text-purple-deep text-2xl leading-tight">Gideon and Manoah</h3><div class="kjt-x mt-3"><blockquote class="kjt-x-v"><p>And the angel of the LORD appeared unto him, and said unto him, The LORD is with thee, thou mighty man of valour. And Gideon said unto him, Oh my Lord, if the LORD be with us, why then is all this befallen us? and where be all his miracles which our fathers told us of, saying, Did not the LORD bring us up from Egypt? but now the LORD hath forsaken us, and delivered us into the hands of the Midianites. And the LORD looked upon him, and said, Go in this thy might, and thou shalt save Israel from the hand of the Midianites: have not I sent thee?</p><cite><a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Judges/6/12-14">Judges 6:12-14</a></cite></blockquote><blockquote class="kjt-x-v"><p>And Manoah said unto the angel of the LORD, What is thy name, that when thy sayings come to pass we may do thee honour? And the angel of the LORD said unto him, Why askest thou thus after my name, seeing it is secret?</p><cite><a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Judges/13/17-18">Judges 13:17-18</a></cite></blockquote><blockquote class="kjt-x-v"><p>But the angel of the LORD did no more appear to Manoah and to his wife. Then Manoah knew that he was an angel of the LORD. And Manoah said unto his wife, We shall surely die, because we have seen God.</p><cite><a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Judges/13/21-22">Judges 13:21-22</a></cite></blockquote><p class="text-ink text-base leading-8">The name He will not tell is “secret”, in Hebrew “wonderful”: the same word as “His name shall be called Wonderful” in Isaiah 9:6. Manoah knows that he has seen God.</p></div></article><article class="border-line rounded-3xl border bg-white p-6 sm:p-7"><h3 class="font-display text-purple-deep text-2xl leading-tight">Every knee shall bow</h3><div class="kjt-x mt-3"><blockquote class="kjt-x-v"><p>Look unto me, and be ye saved, all the ends of the earth: for I am God, and there is none else. I have sworn by myself, the word is gone out of my mouth in righteousness, and shall not return, That unto me every knee shall bow, every tongue shall swear.</p><cite><a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Isaiah/45/22-23">Isaiah 45:22-23</a></cite></blockquote><blockquote class="kjt-x-v"><p>Wherefore God also hath highly exalted him, and given him a name which is above every name: That at the name of Jesus every knee should bow, of things in heaven, and things in earth, and things under the earth; And that every tongue should confess that Jesus Christ is Lord, to the glory of God the Father.</p><cite><a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Philippians/2/9-11">Philippians 2:9-11</a></cite></blockquote><p class="text-ink text-base leading-8">What God says of Himself in Isaiah, St Paul says of Jesus: to Him every knee shall bow.</p></div></article><article class="border-line rounded-3xl border bg-white p-6 sm:p-7"><h3 class="font-display text-purple-deep text-2xl leading-tight">One God, one Lord</h3><div class="kjt-x mt-3"><blockquote class="kjt-x-v"><p>Hear, O Israel: The LORD our God is one LORD:</p><cite><a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Deuteronomy/6/4">Deuteronomy 6:4</a></cite></blockquote><blockquote class="kjt-x-v"><p>But to us there is but one God, the Father, of whom are all things, and we in him; and one Lord Jesus Christ, by whom are all things, and we by him.</p><cite><a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/1%20Corinthians/8/6">1 Corinthians 8:6</a></cite></blockquote><p class="text-ink text-base leading-8">St Paul confesses the faith of Israel, “the LORD our God is one LORD”, and names in it the Father and the Lord Jesus Christ.</p></div></article></div><div class="kjt-x kjt-x-tail"><p class="kjt-x-src">St Justin Martyr (2nd century) shows from these passages that the One who appeared to Abraham, Jacob and Moses is the Son: Dialogue with Trypho, chapters 56 to 62. <a href="https://www.newadvent.org/fathers/0128.htm" rel="noopener" target="_blank">newadvent.org</a></p></div></div></section><section class="kjt-gen scroll-mt-20" id="genealogy" aria-labelledby="kjt-gen-h" data-kjt-notr lang="en"><div class="kjt-gen__in"><p class="kjt-gen__eyebrow">The Son of David, the Son of Abraham</p><h2 class="kjt-gen__h" id="kjt-gen-h">The genealogy of Christ</h2><p class="kjt-gen__lead">“The book of the generation of Jesus Christ, the son of David, the son of Abraham” <a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-gen__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Matthew/1/1">Matthew 1:1</a>. God promised Abraham that in his seed all the nations of the earth would be blessed <a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-gen__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Genesis/22/18">Genesis 22:18</a>, and David that a righteous Branch would be raised to him <a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-gen__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Jeremiah/23/5">Jeremiah 23:5</a> <a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-gen__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Isaiah/11/1">Isaiah 11:1</a>. Saint Matthew and Saint Luke show that Jesus is that Son, the heir of every promise.</p><figure class="kjt-gen__fig kjt-gen__fig--wide"><a href="https://knowingjesus.today/wp-content/plugins/kjt-site-pictures/assets/god-with-us/genealogy-linked.webp?ver=7.48.0" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><img src="https://knowingjesus.today/wp-content/plugins/kjt-site-pictures/assets/god-with-us/genealogy-linked.webp?ver=7.48.0" width="900" height="675" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="How the two genealogies of Christ are linked: Saint Matthew’s line through Solomon and Saint Luke’s through Nathan, both from King David"></a><figcaption><a href="https://knowingjesus.today/wp-content/plugins/kjt-site-pictures/assets/god-with-us/genealogy-linked.webp?ver=7.48.0" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open the full picture ↗</a></figcaption></figure><div class="kjt-gen__two"><article class="kjt-gen__card"><figure class="kjt-gen__fig "><a href="https://knowingjesus.today/wp-content/plugins/kjt-site-pictures/assets/god-with-us/genealogy-matthew.webp?ver=7.48.0" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><img src="https://knowingjesus.today/wp-content/plugins/kjt-site-pictures/assets/god-with-us/genealogy-matthew.webp?ver=7.48.0" width="900" height="1272" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="Saint Matthew: through Solomon"></a><figcaption><a href="https://knowingjesus.today/wp-content/plugins/kjt-site-pictures/assets/god-with-us/genealogy-matthew.webp?ver=7.48.0" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open the full picture ↗</a></figcaption></figure><h3>Saint Matthew: through Solomon</h3><p>From Abraham down to Christ, through Solomon and the kings of Judah: three times fourteen generations <a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-gen__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Matthew/1/17">Matthew 1:17</a>. Saint Matthew wrote for the Jews, and shows the King, the heir of David’s throne. Here Joseph is the son of Jacob by nature <a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-gen__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Matthew/1/16">Matthew 1:16</a>.</p></article><article class="kjt-gen__card"><figure class="kjt-gen__fig "><a href="https://knowingjesus.today/wp-content/plugins/kjt-site-pictures/assets/god-with-us/genealogy-luke.webp?ver=7.48.0" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><img src="https://knowingjesus.today/wp-content/plugins/kjt-site-pictures/assets/god-with-us/genealogy-luke.webp?ver=7.48.0" width="900" height="1272" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="Saint Luke: through Nathan"></a><figcaption><a href="https://knowingjesus.today/wp-content/plugins/kjt-site-pictures/assets/god-with-us/genealogy-luke.webp?ver=7.48.0" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open the full picture ↗</a></figcaption></figure><h3>Saint Luke: through Nathan</h3><p>From Christ back to Adam, “which was the son of God” <a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-gen__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Luke/3/38">Luke 3:38</a>, through Nathan, another son of David. Saint Luke wrote for all nations, and shows Christ, the new Adam, the Saviour of every man. Here Joseph is the son of Heli by law <a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-gen__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Luke/3/23">Luke 3:23</a>.</p></article></div><div class="kjt-gen__boxes"><div class="kjt-gen__box"><h3>Why two genealogies?</h3><p>The holy Fathers explain it by the Law of Moses: when a man died without children, his brother married the widow, and the first son was counted as the dead man’s son <a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-gen__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Deuteronomy/25/5-6">Deuteronomy 25:5-6</a>. Jacob (in Matthew) and Heli (in Luke) were brothers by one mother, of two branches of David’s house. Heli died childless, and Jacob raised up seed to his brother. So Joseph was the son of Jacob by nature, and the son of Heli by law: both Gospels are true. This is the teaching of Saint Julius Africanus, kept by Eusebius and by Saint John of Damascus.</p></div><div class="kjt-gen__box kjt-gen__box--mary"><h3>And the Most Holy Theotokos?</h3><p>The genealogies name Joseph, because the Law counted a family through the father, and in the eyes of all Joseph was the lawful father of Jesus <a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-gen__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Luke/3/23">Luke 3:23</a>. The Virgin herself is of the house of David: Christ is “made of the seed of David according to the flesh” <a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-gen__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Romans/1/3">Romans 1:3</a>, and the Lord God gives Him “the throne of his father David” <a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-gen__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Luke/1/32">Luke 1:32</a>. Holy Tradition names her parents, the righteous Joachim and Anna, of the tribe of Judah and the house of David. So Christ is the Son of David in the flesh, born of the Virgin, and the heir of David’s throne through Joseph.</p></div></div><p class="kjt-gen__end">“I am the root and the offspring of David, and the bright and morning star.” <a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-gen__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Revelation/22/16">Revelation 22:16</a></p></div></section><section class="bg-white border-line border-t scroll-mt-20 kjt-x-sec" id="nativity"><div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-5 py-14 sm:px-8 sm:py-20"><div class="mb-10 max-w-3xl"><p class="text-purple text-xs font-bold tracking-[0.22em] uppercase">The Nativity of Christ</p><h2 class="font-display text-purple-deep mt-3 text-4xl leading-tight sm:text-5xl">The Word was made flesh</h2><p class="text-ink mt-5 text-lg leading-8">St Matthew and St Luke tell of the birth of Christ. Here it is in order, with what the prophets foretold. The Church celebrates it on 25 December (7 January in the churches that keep the old calendar).</p></div><div class="kjt-x-grid grid gap-5"><article class="border-line rounded-3xl border bg-white p-6 sm:p-7"><h3 class="font-display text-purple-deep text-2xl leading-tight">The Annunciation</h3><div class="kjt-x mt-3"><blockquote class="kjt-x-v"><p>And the angel said unto her, Fear not, Mary: for thou hast found favour with God. And, behold, thou shalt conceive in thy womb, and bring forth a son, and shalt call his name JESUS. He shall be great, and shall be called the Son of the Highest: and the Lord God shall give unto him the throne of his father David: And he shall reign over the house of Jacob for ever; and of his kingdom there shall be no end. Then said Mary unto the angel, How shall this be, seeing I know not a man? And the angel answered and said unto her, The Holy Ghost shall come upon thee, and the power of the Highest shall overshadow thee: therefore also that holy thing which shall be born of thee shall be called the Son of God.</p><cite><a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Luke/1/30-35">Luke 1:30-35</a></cite></blockquote><p class="text-ink text-base leading-8">The Archangel Gabriel is sent to the Virgin Mary in Nazareth. She answers: “Behold the handmaid of the Lord; be it unto me according to thy word” (Luke 1:38).</p></div></article><article class="border-line rounded-3xl border bg-white p-6 sm:p-7"><h3 class="font-display text-purple-deep text-2xl leading-tight">Joseph’s dream</h3><div class="kjt-x mt-3"><blockquote class="kjt-x-v"><p>But while he thought on these things, behold, the angel of the Lord appeared unto him in a dream, saying, Joseph, thou son of David, fear not to take unto thee Mary thy wife: for that which is conceived in her is of the Holy Ghost. And she shall bring forth a son, and thou shalt call his name JESUS: for he shall save his people from their sins. Now all this was done, that it might be fulfilled which was spoken of the Lord by the prophet, saying, Behold, a virgin shall be with child, and shall bring forth a son, and they shall call his name Emmanuel, which being interpreted is, God with us.</p><cite><a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Matthew/1/20-23">Matthew 1:20-23</a></cite></blockquote><p class="text-ink text-base leading-8">Joseph, a righteous man, meant to put her away quietly. The angel tells him that the Child is of the Holy Spirit, and gives His name: Jesus, “the Lord saves”.</p></div></article><article class="border-line rounded-3xl border bg-white p-6 sm:p-7"><h3 class="font-display text-purple-deep text-2xl leading-tight">Born in Bethlehem, laid in a manger</h3><div class="kjt-x mt-3"><blockquote class="kjt-x-v"><p>And Joseph also went up from Galilee, out of the city of Nazareth, into Judæa, unto the city of David, which is called Bethlehem; (because he was of the house and lineage of David:) To be taxed with Mary his espoused wife, being great with child. And so it was, that, while they were there, the days were accomplished that she should be delivered. And she brought forth her firstborn son, and wrapped him in swaddling clothes, and laid him in a manger; because there was no room for them in the inn.</p><cite><a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Luke/2/4-7">Luke 2:4-7</a></cite></blockquote><p class="text-ink text-base leading-8">A census of Caesar Augustus brings Joseph, of the house of David, to Bethlehem, as Micah foretold. There was no room in the inn. The icon of the Nativity shows a cave, with the ox and the ass of Isaiah: “The ox knoweth his owner, and the ass his master’s crib” (Isaiah 1:3).</p></div></article><article class="border-line rounded-3xl border bg-white p-6 sm:p-7"><h3 class="font-display text-purple-deep text-2xl leading-tight">The shepherds and the angels</h3><div class="kjt-x mt-3"><blockquote class="kjt-x-v"><p>And the angel said unto them, Fear not: for, behold, I bring you good tidings of great joy, which shall be to all people. For unto you is born this day in the city of David a Saviour, which is Christ the Lord. And this shall be a sign unto you; Ye shall find the babe wrapped in swaddling clothes, lying in a manger. And suddenly there was with the angel a multitude of the heavenly host praising God, and saying, Glory to God in the highest, and on earth peace, good will toward men.</p><cite><a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Luke/2/10-14">Luke 2:10-14</a></cite></blockquote><p class="text-ink text-base leading-8">The first to hear are poor shepherds keeping watch by night. They go, find the Child, and tell everyone what they have seen.</p></div></article><article class="border-line rounded-3xl border bg-white p-6 sm:p-7"><h3 class="font-display text-purple-deep text-2xl leading-tight">The name, and the Presentation in the Temple</h3><div class="kjt-x mt-3"><blockquote class="kjt-x-v"><p>And when eight days were accomplished for the circumcising of the child, his name was called JESUS, which was so named of the angel before he was conceived in the womb.</p><cite><a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Luke/2/21">Luke 2:21</a></cite></blockquote><blockquote class="kjt-x-v"><p>Lord, now lettest thou thy servant depart in peace, according to thy word: For mine eyes have seen thy salvation, Which thou hast prepared before the face of all people; A light to lighten the Gentiles, and the glory of thy people Israel.</p><cite><a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Luke/2/29-32">Luke 2:29-32</a></cite></blockquote><p class="text-ink text-base leading-8">On the eighth day He is named Jesus; on the fortieth He is brought to the Temple, where the elder Simeon takes Him in his arms.</p></div></article><article class="border-line rounded-3xl border bg-white p-6 sm:p-7"><h3 class="font-display text-purple-deep text-2xl leading-tight">The Magi and the star</h3><div class="kjt-x mt-3"><blockquote class="kjt-x-v"><p>Now when Jesus was born in Bethlehem of Judaea in the days of Herod the king, behold, there came wise men from the east to Jerusalem, Saying, Where is he that is born King of the Jews? for we have seen his star in the east, and are come to worship him.</p><cite><a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Matthew/2/1-2">Matthew 2:1-2</a></cite></blockquote><blockquote class="kjt-x-v"><p>And when they were come into the house, they saw the young child with Mary his mother, and fell down, and worshipped him: and when they had opened their treasures, they presented unto him gifts; gold, and frankincense, and myrrh.</p><cite><a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Matthew/2/11">Matthew 2:11</a></cite></blockquote><p class="text-ink text-base leading-8">Wise men from the East, Gentiles, are the first of the nations to worship Him. Gold for a King, frankincense for God, myrrh for the One who would die.</p></div></article><article class="border-line rounded-3xl border bg-white p-6 sm:p-7"><h3 class="font-display text-purple-deep text-2xl leading-tight">The flight into Egypt</h3><div class="kjt-x mt-3"><blockquote class="kjt-x-v"><p>And when they were departed, behold, the angel of the Lord appeareth to Joseph in a dream, saying, Arise, and take the young child and his mother, and flee into Egypt, and be thou there until I bring thee word: for Herod will seek the young child to destroy him. When he arose, he took the young child and his mother by night, and departed into Egypt: And was there until the death of Herod: that it might be fulfilled which was spoken of the Lord by the prophet, saying, Out of Egypt have I called my son.</p><cite><a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Matthew/2/13-15">Matthew 2:13-15</a></cite></blockquote><blockquote class="kjt-x-v"><p>Then Herod, when he saw that he was mocked of the wise men, was exceeding wroth, and sent forth, and slew all the children that were in Bethlehem, and in all the coasts thereof, from two years old and under, according to the time which he had diligently enquired of the wise men.</p><cite><a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Matthew/2/16">Matthew 2:16</a></cite></blockquote><p class="text-ink text-base leading-8">Herod kills the children of Bethlehem, the Holy Innocents, remembered by the Church on 29 December. After Herod’s death the Holy Family returns and lives in Nazareth (Matthew 2:19-23).</p></div></article></div><div class="kjt-x kjt-x-tail"><h3 class="kjt-x-h">Prophecies fulfilled at His birth</h3><ul class="kjt-x-l kjt-x-pf"><li><strong>Born of a virgin</strong> &middot; <a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Isaiah/7/14">Isaiah 7:14</a> <span aria-hidden="true">→</span> <a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Matthew/1/22-23">Matthew 1:22-23</a></li><li><strong>Of the house of David</strong> &middot; <a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/2%20Samuel/7/12-13">2 Samuel 7:12-13</a> <span aria-hidden="true">→</span> <a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Luke/1/32-33">Luke 1:32-33</a></li><li><strong>In Bethlehem</strong> &middot; <a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Micah/5/2">Micah 5:2</a> <span aria-hidden="true">→</span> <a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Matthew/2/5-6">Matthew 2:5-6</a></li><li><strong>A star out of Jacob</strong> &middot; <a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Numbers/24/17">Numbers 24:17</a> <span aria-hidden="true">→</span> <a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Matthew/2/2">Matthew 2:2</a></li><li><strong>Kings bring gifts and worship Him</strong> &middot; <a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Psalms/72/10-11">Psalms 72:10-11</a> <span aria-hidden="true">→</span> <a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Matthew/2/11">Matthew 2:11</a></li><li><strong>Out of Egypt</strong> &middot; <a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Hosea/11/1">Hosea 11:1</a> <span aria-hidden="true">→</span> <a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Matthew/2/15">Matthew 2:15</a></li><li><strong>Rachel weeping for her children</strong> &middot; <a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Jeremiah/31/15">Jeremiah 31:15</a> <span aria-hidden="true">→</span> <a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Matthew/2/17-18">Matthew 2:17-18</a></li><li><strong>Unto us a child is born</strong> &middot; <a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Isaiah/9/6">Isaiah 9:6</a> <span aria-hidden="true">→</span> <a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Luke/2/11">Luke 2:11</a></li></ul><p class="kjt-x-go"><a href="#prophecies">All the prophecies, in “Jesus Was Foretold from the Beginning”</a></p></div></div></section><section id="words-works" class="kld-section kdt-section kww-section scroll-mt-20" aria-labelledby="kww-title"><div class="kld-wrap"><div class="kld-head"><p class="kld-eyebrow">Deep dive &middot; God with us</p><h2 id="kww-title" class="kld-title">The Words and Works of Christ</h2><p class="kld-intro">Everything He commanded, every parable He told and every miracle He worked, in the order of the Holy Gospels, with the Scriptures that tell them.</p></div><div class="kww-cards"><button type="button" class="kww-card" data-kdt-open="commandments"><span class="kww-card__ic" aria-hidden="true">📜</span><span class="kww-card__t">The commandments of Christ</span><span class="kww-card__s">108 commandments, gathered by subject</span></button><button type="button" class="kww-card" data-kdt-open="parables"><span class="kww-card__ic" aria-hidden="true">🌾</span><span class="kww-card__t">The parables</span><span class="kww-card__s">54 parables, in the order He told them</span></button><button type="button" class="kww-card" data-kdt-open="miracles"><span class="kww-card__ic" aria-hidden="true">✨</span><span class="kww-card__t">The miracles</span><span class="kww-card__s">38 miracles, in the order of the Gospels</span></button><button type="button" class="kww-card" data-kdt-open="signs"><span class="kww-card__ic" aria-hidden="true">🕊️</span><span class="kww-card__t">The seven signs of Saint John</span><span class="kww-card__s">From Cana to the raising of Lazarus</span></button></div><div class="kld-cta"><button type="button" class="kdt-open" data-kdt-open="words">Open the deep dive</button><p class="kld-cta__note">Opens full screen. Tap any reference to read the passage.</p></div></div></section><section class="bg-paper border-line border-t scroll-mt-20 kjt-x-sec" id="holy-week"><div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-5 py-14 sm:px-8 sm:py-20"><div class="mb-10 max-w-3xl"><p class="text-purple text-xs font-bold tracking-[0.22em] uppercase">Holy Week</p><h2 class="font-display text-purple-deep mt-3 text-4xl leading-tight sm:text-5xl">Holy Week, day by day</h2><p class="text-ink mt-5 text-lg leading-8">From Lazarus Saturday to Pascha the Church walks with the Lord, day by day, to His Cross and His Resurrection. Each day, what the Gospels tell and what the Church remembers.</p></div><div class="kjt-x-grid grid gap-5"><article class="border-line rounded-3xl border bg-white p-6 sm:p-7"><h3 class="font-display text-purple-deep text-2xl leading-tight">Lazarus Saturday</h3><div class="kjt-x mt-3"><blockquote class="kjt-x-v"><p>And when he thus had spoken, he cried with a loud voice, Lazarus, come forth. And he that was dead came forth, bound hand and foot with graveclothes: and his face was bound about with a napkin. Jesus saith unto them, Loose him, and let him go.</p><cite><a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/John/11/43-44">John 11:43-44</a></cite></blockquote><p class="text-ink text-base leading-8">Christ raises Lazarus, four days dead, in Bethany: a pledge of the general resurrection, before His own Passion.</p><ul class="kjt-x-l"><li><strong>Read</strong> &middot; <a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/John/11/1-45">John 11:1-45</a></li></ul></div></article><article class="border-line rounded-3xl border bg-white p-6 sm:p-7"><h3 class="font-display text-purple-deep text-2xl leading-tight">Palm Sunday: the Entry into Jerusalem</h3><div class="kjt-x mt-3"><blockquote class="kjt-x-v"><p>Took branches of palm trees, and went forth to meet him, and cried, Hosanna: Blessed is the King of Israel that cometh in the name of the Lord.</p><cite><a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/John/12/13">John 12:13</a></cite></blockquote><p class="text-ink text-base leading-8">He rides into Jerusalem on a donkey, as Zechariah foretold (Zechariah 9:9). The crowds spread palm branches and garments and cry “Hosanna”.</p><ul class="kjt-x-l"><li><strong>Read</strong> &middot; <a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Matthew/21/1-11">Matthew 21:1-11</a></li><li><strong>Read</strong> &middot; <a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Mark/11/1-11">Mark 11:1-11</a></li><li><strong>Read</strong> &middot; <a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Luke/19/28-44">Luke 19:28-44</a></li><li><strong>Read</strong> &middot; <a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/John/12/12-19">John 12:12-19</a></li></ul></div></article><article class="border-line rounded-3xl border bg-white p-6 sm:p-7"><h3 class="font-display text-purple-deep text-2xl leading-tight">Holy Monday</h3><div class="kjt-x mt-3"><p class="text-ink text-base leading-8">He curses the barren fig tree and drives the money changers out of the Temple: “My house shall be called the house of prayer”. The Church also remembers Joseph the all-comely, sold by his brothers, an image of Christ.</p><ul class="kjt-x-l"><li><strong>Read</strong> &middot; <a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Matthew/21/12-22">Matthew 21:12-22</a></li><li><strong>Read</strong> &middot; <a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Mark/11/12-19">Mark 11:12-19</a></li><li><strong>Read</strong> &middot; <a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Luke/19/45-48">Luke 19:45-48</a></li></ul></div></article><article class="border-line rounded-3xl border bg-white p-6 sm:p-7"><h3 class="font-display text-purple-deep text-2xl leading-tight">Holy Tuesday</h3><div class="kjt-x mt-3"><p class="text-ink text-base leading-8">He teaches in the Temple and answers the Pharisees, the Herodians and the Sadducees: the tribute to Caesar, the resurrection, the greatest commandment. On the Mount of Olives He speaks of His coming, and of the ten virgins and the talents, which the Church remembers this day.</p><ul class="kjt-x-l"><li><strong>Read</strong> &middot; <a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Matthew/22/15-46">Matthew 22:15-46</a></li><li><strong>Read</strong> &middot; <a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Matthew/25/1-30">Matthew 25:1-30</a></li><li><strong>Read</strong> &middot; <a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Mark/12/13-40">Mark 12:13-40</a></li><li><strong>Read</strong> &middot; <a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Luke/20/20-47">Luke 20:20-47</a></li></ul></div></article><article class="border-line rounded-3xl border bg-white p-6 sm:p-7"><h3 class="font-display text-purple-deep text-2xl leading-tight">Holy Wednesday</h3><div class="kjt-x mt-3"><p class="text-ink text-base leading-8">In Bethany a woman pours precious ointment on His head, “for my burial”. That same day Judas goes to the chief priests and agrees to betray Him for thirty pieces of silver. The Church sets the repentance of the sinful woman beside the fall of the disciple.</p><ul class="kjt-x-l"><li><strong>Read</strong> &middot; <a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Matthew/26/6-16">Matthew 26:6-16</a></li><li><strong>Read</strong> &middot; <a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Mark/14/3-11">Mark 14:3-11</a></li><li><strong>Read</strong> &middot; <a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Luke/22/1-6">Luke 22:1-6</a></li></ul></div></article><article class="border-line rounded-3xl border bg-white p-6 sm:p-7"><h3 class="font-display text-purple-deep text-2xl leading-tight">Holy Thursday</h3><div class="kjt-x mt-3"><p class="text-ink text-base leading-8">The Mystical Supper: He washes the disciples’ feet and gives them His Body and Blood, the Holy Eucharist. Then He prays in Gethsemane, is betrayed with a kiss, and is arrested.</p><ul class="kjt-x-l"><li><strong>Read</strong> &middot; <a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Matthew/26/17-56">Matthew 26:17-56</a></li><li><strong>Read</strong> &middot; <a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Mark/14/12-52">Mark 14:12-52</a></li><li><strong>Read</strong> &middot; <a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Luke/22/7-53">Luke 22:7-53</a></li><li><strong>Read</strong> &middot; <a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/John/13/1-17">John 13:1-17</a></li></ul></div></article><article class="border-line rounded-3xl border bg-white p-6 sm:p-7"><h3 class="font-display text-purple-deep text-2xl leading-tight">Holy and Great Friday</h3><div class="kjt-x mt-3"><p class="text-ink text-base leading-8">He is judged, mocked and scourged, and crucified between two thieves. He dies on the Cross, and Joseph and Nicodemus lay His body in a new tomb. Hour by hour, below.</p><ul class="kjt-x-l"><li><strong>Read</strong> &middot; <a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Matthew/27/1-61">Matthew 27:1-61</a></li><li><strong>Read</strong> &middot; <a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Mark/15/1-47">Mark 15:1-47</a></li><li><strong>Read</strong> &middot; <a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Luke/23/1-56">Luke 23:1-56</a></li><li><strong>Read</strong> &middot; <a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/John/19/1-42">John 19:1-42</a></li></ul></div></article><article class="border-line rounded-3xl border bg-white p-6 sm:p-7"><h3 class="font-display text-purple-deep text-2xl leading-tight">Holy Saturday</h3><div class="kjt-x mt-3"><blockquote class="kjt-x-v"><p>For Christ also hath once suffered for sins, the just for the unjust, that he might bring us to God, being put to death in the flesh, but quickened by the Spirit: By which also he went and preached unto the spirits in prison;</p><cite><a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/1%20Peter/3/18-19">1 Peter 3:18-19</a></cite></blockquote><p class="text-ink text-base leading-8">His body rests in the tomb on the Sabbath, sealed and guarded. His soul goes down into Hades and frees the righteous who waited for Him: the “blessed Sabbath”.</p><ul class="kjt-x-l"><li><strong>Read</strong> &middot; <a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Matthew/27/62-66">Matthew 27:62-66</a></li></ul></div></article><article class="border-line rounded-3xl border bg-white p-6 sm:p-7"><h3 class="font-display text-purple-deep text-2xl leading-tight">Pascha: the Resurrection</h3><div class="kjt-x mt-3"><blockquote class="kjt-x-v"><p>And as they were afraid, and bowed down their faces to the earth, they said unto them, Why seek ye the living among the dead? He is not here, but is risen: remember how he spake unto you when he was yet in Galilee,</p><cite><a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Luke/24/5-6">Luke 24:5-6</a></cite></blockquote><p class="text-ink text-base leading-8">Early on the first day of the week the myrrh-bearing women find the tomb empty. Christ is risen! He appears to Mary Magdalene and to the apostles, and sends them to all nations.</p><ul class="kjt-x-l"><li><strong>Read</strong> &middot; <a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Matthew/28/1-20">Matthew 28:1-20</a></li><li><strong>Read</strong> &middot; <a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Mark/16/1-20">Mark 16:1-20</a></li><li><strong>Read</strong> &middot; <a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Luke/24/1-53">Luke 24:1-53</a></li><li><strong>Read</strong> &middot; <a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/John/20/1-31">John 20:1-31</a></li></ul></div></article><article class="border-line rounded-3xl border bg-white p-6 sm:p-7 kjt-x-wide"><h3 class="font-display text-purple-deep text-2xl leading-tight">Why the Church fasts on Wednesdays and Fridays</h3><div class="kjt-x mt-3"><p class="text-ink text-base leading-8">Every week the Church remembers Holy Week: on Wednesday, the betrayal of Christ; on Friday, His Crucifixion and death. So Orthodox Christians fast on these two days through most of the year.</p><p class="text-ink text-base leading-8">The custom is as old as the Apostles’ disciples. The Didache, written about the end of the first century, says: “Let not your fasts be with the hypocrites, for they fast on the second and fifth day of the week; but fast on the fourth day and on the Preparation” (that is, Wednesday and Friday). Christ Himself said that His disciples would fast when the Bridegroom was taken from them.</p><blockquote class="kjt-x-v"><p>And Jesus said unto them, Can the children of the bridechamber mourn, as long as the bridegroom is with them? but the days will come, when the bridegroom shall be taken from them, and then shall they fast.</p><cite><a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Matthew/9/15">Matthew 9:15</a></cite></blockquote><p class="text-ink text-base leading-8">Fasting is not a punishment but a help: it trains the will, makes room for prayer and almsgiving, and strengthens us against temptation.</p></div></article></div></div></section><section class="kjt-pa scroll-mt-20" id="passion" aria-labelledby="kjt-pa-h"><div class="kjt-pa__in"><p class="kjt-pa__eyebrow">Holy Week</p><h2 class="kjt-pa__h" id="kjt-pa-h">The Passion, hour by hour</h2><p class="kjt-pa__lead">From the Mystical Supper to the Resurrection, as the four Holy Gospels tell it. The Jews counted the hours of the day from sunrise: the third hour is about nine in the morning, the sixth about noon, the ninth about three in the afternoon.</p><ol class="kjt-pa__tl"><li class="kjt-pa__g kjt-pa__g--day"><div class="kjt-pa__when"><span class="kjt-pa__dot" aria-hidden="true"></span><p class="kjt-pa__w">Thursday evening</p><p class="kjt-pa__day">Holy Thursday</p></div><ol class="kjt-pa__ev"><li><h4>The Mystical Supper</h4><p>At the Passover He washes the disciples’ feet, gives them His Body and Blood, and foretells Judas’ betrayal and Peter’s denial.</p><p class="kjt-pa__r"><a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-cx__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Matthew/26/20-30" title="Read it in the Bible">Matthew 26:20-30</a><span aria-hidden="true"> · </span><a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-cx__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Mark/14/17-26" title="Read it in the Bible">Mark 14:17-26</a><span aria-hidden="true"> · </span><a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-cx__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Luke/22/14-38" title="Read it in the Bible">Luke 22:14-38</a><span aria-hidden="true"> · </span><a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-cx__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/John/13/1-30" title="Read it in the Bible">John 13:1-30</a></p></li><li><h4>The farewell discourse and His prayer to the Father</h4><p>He speaks to them of the Comforter and prays that they may all be one.</p><p class="kjt-pa__r"><a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-cx__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/John/14/1-31" title="Read it in the Bible">John 14:1-31</a><span aria-hidden="true"> · </span><a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-cx__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/John/17/1-26" title="Read it in the Bible">John 17:1-26</a></p></li></ol></li><li class="kjt-pa__g"><div class="kjt-pa__when"><span class="kjt-pa__dot" aria-hidden="true"></span><p class="kjt-pa__w">Thursday night</p></div><ol class="kjt-pa__ev"><li><h4>The agony in Gethsemane</h4><p>Not My will, but Thine, be done. His sweat is as great drops of blood.</p><p class="kjt-pa__r"><a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-cx__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Matthew/26/36-46" title="Read it in the Bible">Matthew 26:36-46</a><span aria-hidden="true"> · </span><a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-cx__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Mark/14/32-42" title="Read it in the Bible">Mark 14:32-42</a><span aria-hidden="true"> · </span><a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-cx__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Luke/22/39-46" title="Read it in the Bible">Luke 22:39-46</a></p></li><li><h4>Betrayed with a kiss and arrested</h4><p>Judas comes with a band of soldiers; Peter cuts off Malchus’ ear, and the Lord heals it. All the disciples forsake Him and flee.</p><p class="kjt-pa__r"><a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-cx__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Matthew/26/47-56" title="Read it in the Bible">Matthew 26:47-56</a><span aria-hidden="true"> · </span><a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-cx__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Mark/14/43-52" title="Read it in the Bible">Mark 14:43-52</a><span aria-hidden="true"> · </span><a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-cx__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Luke/22/47-53" title="Read it in the Bible">Luke 22:47-53</a><span aria-hidden="true"> · </span><a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-cx__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/John/18/1-12" title="Read it in the Bible">John 18:1-12</a></p></li><li><h4>Before Annas and Caiaphas</h4><p>False witnesses are sought; He confesses that He is the Christ, the Son of God, and is condemned for blasphemy, spat upon and struck.</p><p class="kjt-pa__r"><a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-cx__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/John/18/13-24" title="Read it in the Bible">John 18:13-24</a><span aria-hidden="true"> · </span><a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-cx__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Matthew/26/57-68" title="Read it in the Bible">Matthew 26:57-68</a><span aria-hidden="true"> · </span><a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-cx__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Mark/14/53-65" title="Read it in the Bible">Mark 14:53-65</a></p></li><li><h4>Peter denies Him three times</h4><p>Before the cock crows; the Lord turns and looks upon Peter, and he goes out and weeps bitterly.</p><p class="kjt-pa__r"><a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-cx__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Matthew/26/69-75" title="Read it in the Bible">Matthew 26:69-75</a><span aria-hidden="true"> · </span><a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-cx__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Luke/22/54-62" title="Read it in the Bible">Luke 22:54-62</a><span aria-hidden="true"> · </span><a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-cx__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/John/18/25-27" title="Read it in the Bible">John 18:25-27</a></p></li></ol></li><li class="kjt-pa__g kjt-pa__g--day"><div class="kjt-pa__when"><span class="kjt-pa__dot" aria-hidden="true"></span><p class="kjt-pa__w">Friday at daybreak</p><p class="kjt-pa__day">Great and Holy Friday</p></div><ol class="kjt-pa__ev"><li><h4>The council condemns Him</h4><p>When the morning is come, the chief priests and elders take counsel to put Him to death.</p><p class="kjt-pa__r"><a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-cx__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Matthew/27/1-2" title="Read it in the Bible">Matthew 27:1-2</a><span aria-hidden="true"> · </span><a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-cx__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Mark/15/1" title="Read it in the Bible">Mark 15:1</a><span aria-hidden="true"> · </span><a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-cx__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Luke/22/66-71" title="Read it in the Bible">Luke 22:66-71</a></p></li><li><h4>Judas returns the thirty pieces of silver</h4><p>He casts them down in the temple and hangs himself; the potter’s field is bought, as the prophet foretold.</p><p class="kjt-pa__r"><a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-cx__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Matthew/27/3-10" title="Read it in the Bible">Matthew 27:3-10</a></p></li><li><h4>Before Pilate</h4><p>Art thou the King of the Jews? My kingdom is not of this world. Pilate finds no fault in Him.</p><p class="kjt-pa__r"><a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-cx__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Matthew/27/11-14" title="Read it in the Bible">Matthew 27:11-14</a><span aria-hidden="true"> · </span><a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-cx__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Luke/23/1-5" title="Read it in the Bible">Luke 23:1-5</a><span aria-hidden="true"> · </span><a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-cx__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/John/18/28-38" title="Read it in the Bible">John 18:28-38</a></p></li><li><h4>Sent to Herod and back</h4><p>He answers Herod nothing; Herod and his soldiers mock Him in a gorgeous robe and send Him back to Pilate.</p><p class="kjt-pa__r"><a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-cx__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Luke/23/6-12" title="Read it in the Bible">Luke 23:6-12</a></p></li><li><h4>Barabbas is released; He is scourged</h4><p>The crowd asks for Barabbas. He is scourged, crowned with thorns and mocked: Behold the man!</p><p class="kjt-pa__r"><a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-cx__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Matthew/27/15-31" title="Read it in the Bible">Matthew 27:15-31</a><span aria-hidden="true"> · </span><a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-cx__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Mark/15/6-20" title="Read it in the Bible">Mark 15:6-20</a><span aria-hidden="true"> · </span><a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-cx__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/John/19/1-15" title="Read it in the Bible">John 19:1-15</a></p></li><li><h4>Condemned to be crucified</h4><p>It was the preparation of the passover; Pilate delivers Him to be crucified. (Saint John says “about the sixth hour”: he counts the hours differently from Saint Mark, and the holy Fathers explain this in more than one way.)</p><p class="kjt-pa__r"><a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-cx__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/John/19/14-16" title="Read it in the Bible">John 19:14-16</a></p></li><li><h4>The way to Golgotha</h4><p>Simon of Cyrene is made to carry His cross; He speaks to the daughters of Jerusalem who weep for Him.</p><p class="kjt-pa__r"><a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-cx__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Matthew/27/32" title="Read it in the Bible">Matthew 27:32</a><span aria-hidden="true"> · </span><a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-cx__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Mark/15/21" title="Read it in the Bible">Mark 15:21</a><span aria-hidden="true"> · </span><a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-cx__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Luke/23/26-32" title="Read it in the Bible">Luke 23:26-32</a><span aria-hidden="true"> · </span><a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-cx__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/John/19/17" title="Read it in the Bible">John 19:17</a></p></li></ol></li><li class="kjt-pa__g"><div class="kjt-pa__when"><span class="kjt-pa__dot" aria-hidden="true"></span><p class="kjt-pa__w">The third hour (about 9 am)</p></div><ol class="kjt-pa__ev"><li><h4>He is crucified</h4><p>“It was the third hour, and they crucified him”, between two thieves. Above Him is written: Jesus of Nazareth, the King of the Jews.</p><p class="kjt-pa__r"><a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-cx__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Mark/15/22-28" title="Read it in the Bible">Mark 15:22-28</a><span aria-hidden="true"> · </span><a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-cx__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/John/19/17-22" title="Read it in the Bible">John 19:17-22</a><span aria-hidden="true"> · </span><a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-cx__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Luke/23/33" title="Read it in the Bible">Luke 23:33</a></p></li><li><h4>Father, forgive them; for they know not what they do</h4><p>The first of His words from the Cross.</p><p class="kjt-pa__r"><a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-cx__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Luke/23/34" title="Read it in the Bible">Luke 23:34</a></p></li><li><h4>They part His garments, casting lots</h4><p>As Psalm 22 foretold.</p><p class="kjt-pa__r"><a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-cx__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/John/19/23-24" title="Read it in the Bible">John 19:23-24</a><span aria-hidden="true"> · </span><a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-cx__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Matthew/27/35" title="Read it in the Bible">Matthew 27:35</a></p></li><li><h4>He is mocked</h4><p>The passers-by, the chief priests and the soldiers mock Him: He saved others; himself he cannot save.</p><p class="kjt-pa__r"><a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-cx__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Matthew/27/39-44" title="Read it in the Bible">Matthew 27:39-44</a><span aria-hidden="true"> · </span><a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-cx__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Mark/15/29-32" title="Read it in the Bible">Mark 15:29-32</a><span aria-hidden="true"> · </span><a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-cx__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Luke/23/35-37" title="Read it in the Bible">Luke 23:35-37</a></p></li><li><h4>The good thief</h4><p>To day shalt thou be with me in paradise.</p><p class="kjt-pa__r"><a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-cx__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Luke/23/39-43" title="Read it in the Bible">Luke 23:39-43</a></p></li><li><h4>Woman, behold thy son! Behold thy mother!</h4><p>He gives His mother to Saint John, and John to her.</p><p class="kjt-pa__r"><a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-cx__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/John/19/25-27" title="Read it in the Bible">John 19:25-27</a></p></li></ol></li><li class="kjt-pa__g"><div class="kjt-pa__when"><span class="kjt-pa__dot" aria-hidden="true"></span><p class="kjt-pa__w">The sixth hour (about noon)</p></div><ol class="kjt-pa__ev"><li><h4>Darkness over all the land</h4><p>From the sixth hour until the ninth hour, the sun is darkened.</p><p class="kjt-pa__r"><a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-cx__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Matthew/27/45" title="Read it in the Bible">Matthew 27:45</a><span aria-hidden="true"> · </span><a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-cx__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Mark/15/33" title="Read it in the Bible">Mark 15:33</a><span aria-hidden="true"> · </span><a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-cx__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Luke/23/44-45" title="Read it in the Bible">Luke 23:44-45</a></p></li></ol></li><li class="kjt-pa__g"><div class="kjt-pa__when"><span class="kjt-pa__dot" aria-hidden="true"></span><p class="kjt-pa__w">The ninth hour (about 3 pm)</p></div><ol class="kjt-pa__ev"><li><h4>My God, my God, why hast thou forsaken me?</h4><p>He cries with a loud voice the first words of Psalm 22.</p><p class="kjt-pa__r"><a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-cx__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Matthew/27/46-47" title="Read it in the Bible">Matthew 27:46-47</a><span aria-hidden="true"> · </span><a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-cx__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Mark/15/34-35" title="Read it in the Bible">Mark 15:34-35</a></p></li><li><h4>I thirst</h4><p>They give Him vinegar on a sponge, upon hyssop.</p><p class="kjt-pa__r"><a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-cx__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/John/19/28-29" title="Read it in the Bible">John 19:28-29</a></p></li><li><h4>It is finished</h4><p class="kjt-pa__r"><a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-cx__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/John/19/30" title="Read it in the Bible">John 19:30</a></p></li><li><h4>Father, into thy hands I commend my spirit</h4><p>He bows His head and gives up the ghost.</p><p class="kjt-pa__r"><a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-cx__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Luke/23/46" title="Read it in the Bible">Luke 23:46</a><span aria-hidden="true"> · </span><a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-cx__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Matthew/27/50" title="Read it in the Bible">Matthew 27:50</a><span aria-hidden="true"> · </span><a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-cx__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Mark/15/37" title="Read it in the Bible">Mark 15:37</a></p></li><li><h4>The veil rent, the earth quakes, the graves are opened</h4><p>The veil of the temple is rent in twain from the top to the bottom; the rocks rend.</p><p class="kjt-pa__r"><a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-cx__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Matthew/27/51-53" title="Read it in the Bible">Matthew 27:51-53</a><span aria-hidden="true"> · </span><a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-cx__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Mark/15/38" title="Read it in the Bible">Mark 15:38</a></p></li><li><h4>Truly this was the Son of God</h4><p>So says the centurion, and the people return smiting their breasts.</p><p class="kjt-pa__r"><a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-cx__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Matthew/27/54" title="Read it in the Bible">Matthew 27:54</a><span aria-hidden="true"> · </span><a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-cx__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Mark/15/39" title="Read it in the Bible">Mark 15:39</a><span aria-hidden="true"> · </span><a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-cx__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Luke/23/47-48" title="Read it in the Bible">Luke 23:47-48</a></p></li></ol></li><li class="kjt-pa__g"><div class="kjt-pa__when"><span class="kjt-pa__dot" aria-hidden="true"></span><p class="kjt-pa__w">Friday afternoon, before sunset</p></div><ol class="kjt-pa__ev"><li><h4>His side is pierced</h4><p>The soldiers break the legs of the thieves, but not His; a soldier pierces His side, and forthwith comes there out blood and water.</p><p class="kjt-pa__r"><a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-cx__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/John/19/31-37" title="Read it in the Bible">John 19:31-37</a></p></li><li><h4>Taken down and laid in the tomb</h4><p>Joseph of Arimathea and Nicodemus wrap His body in linen with spices and lay it in a new tomb; the women see where He is laid.</p><p class="kjt-pa__r"><a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-cx__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Matthew/27/57-61" title="Read it in the Bible">Matthew 27:57-61</a><span aria-hidden="true"> · </span><a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-cx__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Mark/15/42-47" title="Read it in the Bible">Mark 15:42-47</a><span aria-hidden="true"> · </span><a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-cx__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Luke/23/50-56" title="Read it in the Bible">Luke 23:50-56</a><span aria-hidden="true"> · </span><a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-cx__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/John/19/38-42" title="Read it in the Bible">John 19:38-42</a></p></li></ol></li><li class="kjt-pa__g kjt-pa__g--day"><div class="kjt-pa__when"><span class="kjt-pa__dot" aria-hidden="true"></span><p class="kjt-pa__w">Saturday</p><p class="kjt-pa__day">Great and Holy Saturday</p></div><ol class="kjt-pa__ev"><li><h4>The tomb sealed and guarded</h4><p>The chief priests set a watch and seal the stone. His body rests in the tomb, while He descends into Hades to free the righteous.</p><p class="kjt-pa__r"><a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-cx__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Matthew/27/62-66" title="Read it in the Bible">Matthew 27:62-66</a><span aria-hidden="true"> · </span><a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-cx__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/1%20Peter/3/18-19" title="Read it in the Bible">1 Peter 3:18-19</a></p></li></ol></li><li class="kjt-pa__g kjt-pa__g--day"><div class="kjt-pa__when"><span class="kjt-pa__dot" aria-hidden="true"></span><p class="kjt-pa__w">Sunday, very early</p><p class="kjt-pa__day">Holy Pascha</p></div><ol class="kjt-pa__ev"><li><h4>He is risen</h4><p>The myrrh-bearing women find the stone rolled away and the tomb empty: He is not here: for he is risen, as he said.</p><p class="kjt-pa__r"><a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-cx__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Matthew/28/1-10" title="Read it in the Bible">Matthew 28:1-10</a><span aria-hidden="true"> · </span><a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-cx__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Mark/16/1-8" title="Read it in the Bible">Mark 16:1-8</a><span aria-hidden="true"> · </span><a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-cx__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Luke/24/1-12" title="Read it in the Bible">Luke 24:1-12</a><span aria-hidden="true"> · </span><a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-cx__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/John/20/1-18" title="Read it in the Bible">John 20:1-18</a></p></li></ol></li></ol><p class="kjt-pa__more"><a href="#crucifixion">The order of the events on the Cross, with the prophecies ↓</a></p></div></section><section class="kjt-cx scroll-mt-20" id="crucifixion" aria-labelledby="kjt-cx-h"><div class="kjt-cx__in"><p class="kjt-cx__eyebrow">According to the Holy Gospels</p><h2 class="kjt-cx__h" id="kjt-cx-h">The order of the events of the Crucifixion</h2><p class="kjt-cx__lead">Fifteen moments of Great and Holy Friday, in the order the Holy Gospels tell them, with the prophecies of the Old Testament they fulfilled.</p><p class="kjt-see-also"><span class="kjt-see-also__l">See also:</span> <a href="https://knowingjesus.today/know-the-faith/deep-theology/#christ-our-passover">Christ our Passover</a></p><blockquote class="kjt-cx__creed"><span>“And He was crucified for us under Pontius Pilate, and suffered, and was buried.”</span> <cite>The Creed of Faith</cite></blockquote><figure class="kjt-cx__fig"><a class="kjt-cx__zoom" href="https://knowingjesus.today/wp-content/plugins/kjt-site-pictures/assets/god-with-us/crucifixion-order.jpg?ver=7.48.0" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><img src="https://knowingjesus.today/wp-content/plugins/kjt-site-pictures/assets/god-with-us/crucifixion-order-900.jpg?ver=7.48.0" srcset="https://knowingjesus.today/wp-content/plugins/kjt-site-pictures/assets/god-with-us/crucifixion-order-900.jpg?ver=7.48.0 900w, https://knowingjesus.today/wp-content/plugins/kjt-site-pictures/assets/god-with-us/crucifixion-order.jpg?ver=7.48.0 1484w" sizes="(min-width: 1100px) 1040px, 100vw" width="1484" height="1060" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="The order of the events of the Crucifixion according to the Holy Gospels: fifteen icons of the Passion of Christ, with the Gospel references and the prophecies, and six other biblical details"></a><figcaption><a class="kjt-cx__open" href="https://knowingjesus.today/wp-content/plugins/kjt-site-pictures/assets/god-with-us/crucifixion-order.jpg?ver=7.48.0" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open the full picture</a></figcaption></figure><ol class="kjt-cx__list"><li class="kjt-cx__item"><span class="kjt-cx__n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="kjt-cx__body"><h4 class="kjt-cx__t">Arrival at Golgotha (Calvary)</h4><p class="kjt-cx__g"><span class="kjt-cx__l">The Gospels:</span> <a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-cx__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Matthew/27/33" title="Read it in the Bible">Matthew 27:33</a><span class="kjt-cx__sep" aria-hidden="true"> · </span><a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-cx__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Mark/15/22" title="Read it in the Bible">Mark 15:22</a><span class="kjt-cx__sep" aria-hidden="true"> · </span><a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-cx__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Luke/23/33" title="Read it in the Bible">Luke 23:33</a><span class="kjt-cx__sep" aria-hidden="true"> · </span><a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-cx__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/John/19/17" title="Read it in the Bible">John 19:17</a></p><p class="kjt-cx__p"><span class="kjt-cx__l kjt-cx__l--p">Type:</span> <a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-cx__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Genesis/22/2" title="Read it in the Bible">Genesis 22:2</a><span class="kjt-cx__sep" aria-hidden="true"> · </span><a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-cx__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Genesis/22/9-14" title="Read it in the Bible">Genesis 22:9-14</a></p></div></li><li class="kjt-cx__item"><span class="kjt-cx__n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="kjt-cx__body"><h4 class="kjt-cx__t">The offer of a benumbing drink</h4><p class="kjt-cx__g"><span class="kjt-cx__l">The Gospels:</span> <a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-cx__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Matthew/27/34" title="Read it in the Bible">Matthew 27:34</a></p><p class="kjt-cx__p"><span class="kjt-cx__l kjt-cx__l--p">Prophecy:</span> <a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-cx__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Psalms/69/21" title="Read it in the Bible">Psalms 69:21</a></p></div></li><li class="kjt-cx__item"><span class="kjt-cx__n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="kjt-cx__body"><h4 class="kjt-cx__t">The crucifixion</h4><p class="kjt-cx__g"><span class="kjt-cx__l">The Gospels:</span> <a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-cx__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Matthew/27/35" title="Read it in the Bible">Matthew 27:35</a></p><p class="kjt-cx__p"><span class="kjt-cx__l kjt-cx__l--p">Prophecy:</span> <a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-cx__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Psalms/22/16" title="Read it in the Bible">Psalms 22:16</a><span class="kjt-cx__sep" aria-hidden="true"> · </span><a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-cx__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Zechariah/12/10" title="Read it in the Bible">Zechariah 12:10</a></p></div></li><li class="kjt-cx__item"><span class="kjt-cx__n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="kjt-cx__body"><h4 class="kjt-cx__t">“Father, forgive them; for they know not what they do.”</h4><p class="kjt-cx__g"><span class="kjt-cx__l">The Gospels:</span> <a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-cx__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Luke/23/34" title="Read it in the Bible">Luke 23:34</a></p><p class="kjt-cx__p"><span class="kjt-cx__l kjt-cx__l--p">Prophecy:</span> <a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-cx__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Isaiah/53/12" title="Read it in the Bible">Isaiah 53:12</a></p></div></li><li class="kjt-cx__item"><span class="kjt-cx__n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="kjt-cx__body"><h4 class="kjt-cx__t">The parting of Christ’s garments</h4><p class="kjt-cx__g"><span class="kjt-cx__l">The Gospels:</span> <a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-cx__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Matthew/27/35" title="Read it in the Bible">Matthew 27:35</a></p><p class="kjt-cx__p"><span class="kjt-cx__l kjt-cx__l--p">Prophecy:</span> <a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-cx__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Psalms/22/18" title="Read it in the Bible">Psalms 22:18</a></p></div></li><li class="kjt-cx__item"><span class="kjt-cx__n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="kjt-cx__body"><h4 class="kjt-cx__t">Jesus mocked</h4><p class="kjt-cx__g"><span class="kjt-cx__l">The Gospels:</span> <a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-cx__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Matthew/27/39-44" title="Read it in the Bible">Matthew 27:39-44</a><span class="kjt-cx__sep" aria-hidden="true"> · </span><a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-cx__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Mark/15/29" title="Read it in the Bible">Mark 15:29</a></p><p class="kjt-cx__p"><span class="kjt-cx__l kjt-cx__l--p">Prophecy:</span> <a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-cx__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Psalms/22/7-8" title="Read it in the Bible">Psalms 22:7-8</a><span class="kjt-cx__sep" aria-hidden="true"> · </span><a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-cx__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Psalms/69/19-20" title="Read it in the Bible">Psalms 69:19-20</a></p></div></li><li class="kjt-cx__item"><span class="kjt-cx__n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="kjt-cx__body"><h4 class="kjt-cx__t">The thieves rail on Him, but one believes</h4><p class="kjt-cx__g"><span class="kjt-cx__l">The Gospels:</span> <a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-cx__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Matthew/27/44" title="Read it in the Bible">Matthew 27:44</a><span class="kjt-cx__sep" aria-hidden="true"> · </span><a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-cx__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Luke/23/39-42" title="Read it in the Bible">Luke 23:39-42</a></p><p class="kjt-cx__p"><span class="kjt-cx__l kjt-cx__l--p">Prophecy:</span> <a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-cx__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Isaiah/53/12" title="Read it in the Bible">Isaiah 53:12</a></p></div></li><li class="kjt-cx__item"><span class="kjt-cx__n" aria-hidden="true">8</span><div class="kjt-cx__body"><h4 class="kjt-cx__t">“To day shalt thou be with me in paradise.”</h4><p class="kjt-cx__g"><span class="kjt-cx__l">The Gospels:</span> <a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-cx__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Luke/23/43" title="Read it in the Bible">Luke 23:43</a></p><p class="kjt-cx__p"><span class="kjt-cx__l kjt-cx__l--p">Prophecy:</span> <a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-cx__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Isaiah/53/11" title="Read it in the Bible">Isaiah 53:11</a><span class="kjt-cx__sep" aria-hidden="true"> · </span><a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-cx__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Isaiah/61/1" title="Read it in the Bible">Isaiah 61:1</a></p></div></li><li class="kjt-cx__item"><span class="kjt-cx__n" aria-hidden="true">9</span><div class="kjt-cx__body"><h4 class="kjt-cx__t">“Woman, behold thy son!” “Behold thy mother!”</h4><p class="kjt-cx__g"><span class="kjt-cx__l">The Gospels:</span> <a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-cx__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/John/19/26-27" title="Read it in the Bible">John 19:26-27</a></p><p class="kjt-cx__p"><span class="kjt-cx__l kjt-cx__l--p">Prophecy:</span> <a cl